# Campaign Slides — Conceptual Art, No Dubai

Applies to every product gallery / carousel campaign (the 12 slides under `public/images/<x>_campaign/`,
CapCut or Seedance plates, EN/RU/AR).

## Hard rule: no Dubai images

- No Dubai or city scenes in any slide: no skyline, Burj Khalifa, towers, streets, traffic, malls,
  office lobbies, heat haze over a road.
- Heat, sun, AC or Gulf context goes in the **words**, never in a location photo.

## The standard is product 39 (and product 12)

Reference set: `public/images/ultra_campaign/s1–s12.jpg`, notes in
`docs/SESSION_CHANGES_2026-09-26_ULTRA_SHIELD_CAMPAIGN.md`.

- **Two colours only**: the pack colour + one concept colour, alternating seamless backgrounds.
- **One visual metaphor per slide**, shot as a surreal minimal studio still (balloon on a ceiling,
  ghost in a director's chair, velvet rope, hourglass). Not stock lifestyle.
- **Witty headline in two levels**, caps, then one short support line with the real fact.
- **Giant numerals** for real doses.
- **Product appears late** (final one or two slides), so there are few label renders to garble.
- People only when the metaphor needs them, framed as art (a prop, a gesture), not a street scene.
- Type: Manrope **Regular**, caps headline ~140 px on 2560, leading 0.92; support 64 px sentence case;
  pack colour on the light colour, white on the pack colour. Final card lists the product and
  credentials and ends SHOP GENOSYS.AE / GENOSYS UAE APP.

Claims still follow `selling-tone.mdc` and the product's source audit.
